<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akal Takht</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Akal Takht is the highest seat of temporal authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikhism</a>, located in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple">Golden Temple</a> complex at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a>. It was established in the early seventeenth century by Guru Hargobind. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> it served as a centre of religious and political assembly and symbolised the link between Sikh faith and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/akal-takht.jpg" alt="Akal Takht" width="320" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paasikivi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AkalTakhtGoldenTempleComplex.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
